<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania 91-day T-bill rate dips.</title>
<headline>Lithuania 91-day T-bill rate dips.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction of Lithuanian Treasury bills fell slightly to 8.22 percent from 8.27 percent on Tuesday although the issue did not sell out, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AVG YIELD  (LAST TIME)  MIN/MAX  ISSUE   BID    SOLD</p>
<p>  91-day    8.22	  8.27	7.0/9.49   50   50.515  43.265</p>
<p>Settlement date for the auction is February 2 and the bills mature on May 8. The next auction is on Tuesday when 40 million litas of 182-day paper will be sold.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
